import unittest


def add(a, b):
    return a + b


def subtract(a, b):
    return a - b


class TestCalculator(unittest.TestCase):

    def test_add(self):
        self.assertEqual(add(2, 3), 5)

    def test_subtract(self):
        self.assertEqual(subtract(5, 3), 2)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    unittest.main()


"""
Test Results:

The tests were successful because both tests passed without any
errors or failures. The first test checked that the add function
correctly adds 2 and 3 together to produce 5. The second test
checked that the subtract function correctly subtracts 3 from 5
to produce 2.

When the test results show "OK", it means that all of the tests
passed and the functions produced the expected results. Unit
